<title>CANADA: NAFTA dairy panel ruling due end November - Goodale.</title>
<headline>NAFTA dairy panel ruling due end November - Goodale.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The final ruling of a Canada-U.S. panel on trade in dairy, eggs and poultry products should be available by the end of November, Canadian Agriculture Minister Ralph Goodale told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;It is scheduled to be available around about the end of November,&quot; Goodale said in a conference call from Rome.</p>
<p>The North American Free Trade Agreement panel's preliminary ruling July 15 found in Canada's favour after that country converted import quotas into tariffs in compliance with World Trade Organization rules.</p>
<p>The U.S. said there should be no tariffs under NAFTA.</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
</text>
